-- title:
--   Kernel of R_Q→ R_{min} is the augmentation ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for the maximal-adic topology), $p$ a natural number, $S_{\min}$ and $Q$ finite sets of natural numbers with every $q\in Q$ prime and not in $S_{\min}$, and $\bar\rho$ a residual two-dimensional Galois representation over the residue field of $\mathcal O$. Let $D_{\min}$ be a universal deformation datum for $\bar\rho$ for the condition "determinant cyclotomic at $p$, strictly ordinary at $p$, unramified outside $S_{\min}$, and unipotent on inertia at every prime $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$", and $D_Q$ one for the condition obtained by allowing ramification in $S_{\min}\cup Q$ while keeping unipotence on inertia at the primes of $S_{\min}$ other than $p$; each datum consists of a complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ with residue field generated by that of $\mathcal O$, a deformation of $\bar\rho$ of the given type, and the universal property, together with absolute irreducibility of $\bar\rho$. Let $\varepsilon : D_Q.R\to D_{\min}.R$ be a local $\mathcal O$-algebra map carrying $D_Q.\rho$ to $D_{\min}.\rho$ up to equivalence after base change. Let $k:\mathbb N\to\mathbb N$, let $\mathrm{cyc}_q$ be characters of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ into $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ describing, for $q\in Q$, the Galois action on $q$-th roots of unity, let $\pi_{\Delta_q}:(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}$ (written multiplicatively) be surjective for $q\in Q$, and let $\chi_q:\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}\to (D_Q.R)^\times$ be characters such that for each $q\in Q$ and each valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit in $P$ there is a basis $b_0,b_1$ of $D_Q.\rho$'s module on which the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ acts by $\chi_q\circ\pi_{\Delta_q}\circ\mathrm{cyc}_q$ and its inverse. Finally let $\iota:\mathcal O[\prod_{q\in Q}\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}]\to D_Q.R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map sending a group element $g$ to $\prod_{q\in Q}\chi_q(g_q)$. Then the kernel of $\varepsilon$ is the ideal generated by the elements $\iota(g)-1$, $g$ ranging over $\prod_{q\in Q}\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}$.
--
--   This is the Taylor–Wiles statement that the relaxation map from the deformation ring of level $S_{\min}\cup Q$ to the minimal one has kernel exactly the augmentation ideal of the group algebra of the diamond-operator group $\Delta_Q=\prod_{q\in Q}\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}$, here in the strictly ordinary setting. It feeds the construction of the patching data used in the modularity lifting theorem, and is cited by the two existence results for patching data at residually modular representations.
